{
  "id": "ss.char.egg",
  "name": "Egg",
  "description": "The unhatched. The same sealed suit, but the incubator version a brood-body is issued before it is done: a rounded shell over the chest and belly in greyed bone, strapped down with a cocoon wrap that crosses it twice, and a helmet dome a size larger than the others' with a crack running down the crown from a hatching that never finished. Its feelers are stubs; it was never given a signal to lose. A pair of Soldier mandibles bound at the elbow rides racked on the back with the jaws rising over the far shoulder — a squire's weapon, thrown so it comes back — and the suit's only colour is the bone of the shell and a pale line in the visor. Same dead core, set into the shell. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
